"created_at":"2026-11-16T11:27:08.399501+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17 10:36:19.000000","foreman_note":"PM-VERIFY 2026-11-17T10:38Z (speclang-pm-2026-11-17-10-01-06, second pass) \u2014 premise RE-CONFIRMED live, and the tag map is now measured in BOTH directions. Published refs: `git ls-remote --tags origin` gives v0.1.0^{} = 676795fc and v1.0.0^{} = 2f2639a8; `git merge-base --is-ancestor <peel> origin/main` exits 1 for both (origin/main = 59b7b26f) \u2014 still unreachable, row stays open. NEW measurement: the LOCAL tag refs in this checkout disagree with the published ones \u2014 refs/tags/v0.1.0 -> ff96a2e9 and refs/tags/v1.0.0 -> f7b4ce7d, and both of those ARE ancestors of origin/main. The annotated tag objects differ too (local 3acb544b vs remote 3d823fc1 for v0.1.0; both carry tagger date 2026-03-22 15:31:37). Consequence for the fix direction: reconciling only the local map is a FALSE CLOSE, because `git describe` here reports v1.0.0-858-ga02736a1 while no consumer of the published repo can see that lineage, and a release cut from this checkout would be refused (tag exists) or force-move a published tag. Scope the repair to the PUBLISHED map (owner-gated: moving published tags needs force-push consent) and treat the local shadow tags as part of the same repair, not as evidence the tags are healthy."}
 {"id":"RELEASE-003","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":"task","complexity":3,"title":"P1 [releng] no repo-owned release path and no available publish channel (0 CI secrets, npm name speclang owned by a third party)","reasoning":"Inventory of /home/kara/speclang at b9bb5042 finds no release tooling: no Makefile release target, no .goreleaser.yml, no Dockerfile, no scripts/release*, no docs/RELEASING*, and .github/workflows contains only ci.yml triggered on push to main/develop and on pull_request (no tag trigger). package.json is the single version surface (1.0.0) and the CLI reads it at bin/speclang:24. Channel probes: gh api repos/dexdat/SpecLang/actions/secrets --jq .total_count returns 0, so no CI job could authenticate a publish; gh release list returns empty, so the forge Release channel has never published; npm view speclang returns 0.1.1 with maintainer speclang <speclangdev@gmail.com>, created 2022-05-13, source github.com/Specific-Language/speclang, i.e. the bare npm name belongs to another project and is unavailable to dexdat; npm whoami on this host returns ENEEDAUTH. Doctrine requires projects to ship a release script plus docs and requires the lane to use the repository-owned path, and neither exists, so a cut today would be an improvised generic fallback through a channel the project does not control - which is also a first publication and therefore needs explicit owner authorization. This row tracks building the release path and resolving the channel, not cutting a release.","acceptance_criteria":"The repository contains a documented release procedure (script or Makefile target plus release docs) that a non-author can follow, and a rehearsal proves it end to end without publishing: the script or dry-run path exits 0, echoes the computed version and the artifact sha256, and the docs name the channel and the credential it needs. Plus one of: a project-controlled npm package name is available and a publish --dry-run succeeds, or the forge Release channel is authorized with a draft release rehearsal that exits 0. The npm name conflict with the third-party package speclang must be resolved explicitly (scope, rename, or documented decision) rather than left implicit.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"c18798e44a30bd4ebfc6aab2b5a01cbce797a7db1e9809feb2297cf6dd18c136"},"capability_tags":["releng","release-tooling","channel"],"created_at":"2026-11-16T11:27:08.437172+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T11:27:08.437172+00:00"}
 {"id":"RELEASE-001","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":"task","complexity":3,"title":"P1 [releng] SpecLang release readiness - NO-GO at b9bb5042 (4 blocking gates; candidate 1.1.0 proposed)","reasoning":"Rolling release-readiness row, first pass of the speclang-releng lane on this board. Certified candidate = origin/main b9bb5042145f9a87de26c667b1b774adde6a0297, re-read from the release-authority remote origin = github.com/dexdat/SpecLang (default branch main per gh repo view; PUBLIC). Census f7b4ce7d..b9bb5042 (baseline = main-lineage commit the local v1.0.0 peels to): 723 no-merge commits, 6 merges, strict parser reconciles 668 conventional + 55 non-conventional = 723. Type buckets chore 377, speclang 91, docs 64, fix 49, board 43, dogfood 10, ci 9, test 6, feat 4. Breaking changes 0. Material split by changed paths: 173 commits touch product paths, 470 bookkeeping-only, 80 residual. Bump rule gives MINOR -> 1.1.0 proposed, NOT authorized. CI on candidate: run 43855424821 exact-SHA success, job Build-test-and-guard all executed steps success; Tier 2 LLM review skipped BY DESIGN (workflow condition is pull_request or develop push). GitReins Tier 1 guard passed inside that CI job; no Tier 2 verdict exists (no .gitreins/history, tasks.yaml last touched 2026-09-26) so GitReins is degraded, not release-grade. DECISION NO-GO on four independent gates: (a) channel - npm name speclang is owned by a third-party publisher (maintainer speclang <speclangdev@gmail.com>, created 2022-05-13, source github.com/Specific-Language/speclang), npm whoami ENEEDAUTH, gh actions secrets total_count=0, and gh release list is EMPTY so the forge Release channel has never published (any cut is a first publication and needs owner authorization); (b) artifact - installing the packed tarball in a clean consumer exits 127 with bash scripts/postinstall-lint-deps.sh No such file or directory because files[] ships 0 scripts/ entries while package.json declares that postinstall, tarball sha256 e9ca26c61eb6a8663025161329245832b93ef06077baab81d28b3ac1814cde16 (this is the live premise and the exact acceptance test of open row UX-001); (c) dependencies - npm audit --omit=dev reports 14 production advisories, 3 critical (simple-git via @simple-git/argv-parser, proxy-addr) and 4 high (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk, body-parser, brace-expansion, zod); (d) tag identity - see RELEASE-002. Version hygiene: package.json 1.0.0, CHANGELOG top section Unreleased empty, last released section 1.0.0 dated 2026-03-31, 173 material commits stale. No repo-owned release tooling exists (no Makefile release target, no goreleaser, no Dockerfile, no scripts/release*, no RELEASING docs, no tag-triggered workflow) so the generic fallback would be git tag plus gh release create. Evidence artifact .coding-hermes/evidence/speclang-releng-2026-11-16-11-07-39/READINESS.md sha256 823b55dc05133b98fe106f218dc9ddef79cbdc34ddfca5246403346102590d07. Nothing was mutated: no tag, no Release, no publish, no remote ref change.","acceptance_criteria":"At the then-current certified origin/main tip a later readiness pass must re-prove all four gates closed: (1) CHANNEL - a distribution target the project controls exists and a non-publishing rehearsal succeeds (scoped npm name publish --dry-run, or gh release create --draft), with the credential count or session cited; (2) ARTIFACT - npm pack then install the tarball in a clean consumer directory must exit 0 with no ENOENT in npm output and node_modules/.bin/speclang --help exits 0 (this is the UX-001 acceptance test); (3) DEPENDENCIES - npm audit --omit=dev reports 0 critical and 0 high; (4) TAG IDENTITY - every remote tag named in the record either satisfies git merge-base --is-ancestor <peel> origin/main or is documented as superseded by a new main-lineage tag. The pass must cite the exact CI run id on the candidate and must not force-move any existing tag.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"5a2ee8a23d46737633b69cd2f56966ebd739b96dbd4bdd447cd